## Task: Full bakeoff grade for 20 mm1m candidates (2026-08-04)

Goal: grade all 20 ~1M candidates with the report-03 protocol (TinyStories,
300 steps, BLiMP/ARC-E/WikiText), merge with the original 5 arch_* results,
update research docs / RESULTS.md / report 12 / report 03 (full tables).

Plan:
[X] Pull TinyStories + eval data; tokenize v4096
[X] mm1m bakeoff via run_experiment (same DEFAULTS as group_arch)
[X] Merge original arch_* + mm1m_* into combined ranking JSON
[X] Update report 12, RESULTS.md, re-rank docs; tests; commit; push; PR
[X] Inline all 20 + merged 25 into report 03 (not just a pointer)

Lessons:
- Selective SSM Python-autograd unrolling is ~300 tok/s; a custom autograd
  scan (TorchScript forward + reverse sweep) reaches ~7k tok/s on CPU.
- At 2.46M TinyStories tokens, ~1.1M Mamba beats ~1.0M dense on val loss;
  report-03 ~1.7M dense still wins the merged board. Looped remains last.
- `mamba_pure` with conv_kernel=4 is identical to `mamba_conv_gate` — set
  pure's conv_kernel=0 to distinguish them.
- Parallel-scan RG-LRU NaNs beyond ~16–32 tokens at init — use sequential
  float32 scan (changes hybrid training numerics).

