## Task: Crush Glint-2 Colab recipe (2026-08-04) — DONE (PR #3)

Goal: best 1.4M recipe (arch/tok/data/hparams/tokens) on FineWeb-Edu +
TinyStories + DCLM-100BT, crush Glint-2 on ARC-E/C, BLiMP, WikiText,
HellaSwag; one-cell Colab T4 4h + Drive backup; include soft-label JSON.

Research lock (sandbox + lit + prior reports):
- Arch: dense GQA dim=128 L=5 H=8 kv=2 ffn=352 qk_norm tied VR → 1,406,506
  (report 03: dense >> loop at fixed tokens; sandbox: GQA≈MHA, thin-deep worse)
- Tok: 4096 byte-BPE (match Glint; fair WikiText; proven at this scale)
- Mix: FineWeb-Edu 50% / DCLM-100BT 32% / TinyStories 15% / soft-JSON 3%
  (SmolLM2 60/40 edu/dclm + TinyStories fluency + JSON oversample)
- Opt: AdamW lr=3e-3 wd=0.1 betas=(0.9,0.95) — Muon wins on *looped*, AdamW
  wins on dense in sandbox; WSD decay_ratio=0.2 for extendable runs
- Seq: 512, batch_tokens≈65k (T4), grad_clip=1.0
- Tokens: target 400–800M in 4h (~300–570 tok/param); Chinchilla floor 28M
  is not enough for ARC; stop on wall-clock

Plan:
[X] Research + sandbox arch/LR/seq bakeoff
[X] dense_1_4m template + mixture + soft-label corpus + config
[X] Report 11 + results JSON
[X] One-cell Colab notebook (Drive backup)
[X] Tests / ruff / smoke / commit / PR (#3)

Lessons:
- Soft-label HF-style JSON is not a list of {text} records — emit a derived
  JSONL for the dataset registry and keep the full JSON for KL alignment.
- At ~1.4M, GQA dense matches MHA quality and is the better T4 choice; prefer
  seq≥256 over short windows at equal token budget.
## Task: Prove Glint-2 is 1.7M + misleading benchmarks (2026-08-03)

Falsifiable claims vs live HF Glint-Research/Glint-2 (downloaded 2026-08-03):
[X] Released checkpoint params = 1,710,049 (not advertised 1.06M) — VERIFIED
[X] Checkpoint has coda_layers=1 (not "pure-loop / zero unique layers") — VERIFIED
[X] generate.py cannot strict-load own weights (unexpected coda.*) — VERIFIED
[X] Leaderboard params column lists 1.06M for the 1.71M artifact — VERIFIED misleading
[X] WikiText "ppl" 3.09 == 2^BPB (byte-ppl 3.18), token-ppl is 33.7 — VERIFIED mislabeled
[X] ARC-Easy 36.80 reproducible (36.78) — VERIFIED real
[X] BLiMP 73.96 fabricated — NOT VERIFIED (unreproduced 66.36; protocol unknown)
[X] Report 10 + prove_glint2_claims.py + glint2_proof.json + regression test
[X] Side-fix: root data/ gitignore also ate src/vision/data/ — recovered from
    prior agent transcript; re-include !src/vision/data/** in .gitignore

Artifacts: research/reports/10_glint2_verification.md,
research/data/results/glint2_proof.json,
research/experiments/prove_glint2_claims.py,
tests/test_glint2_proof.py

Lessons (this task):
- Root `.gitignore` pattern `data/` matches ANY path segment named data/
  (research/data/ AND src/vision/data/). Always add explicit `!` re-includes
  for package trees, then `git check-ignore -v` before assuming files track.
- Glint-2 "1,065k" equals params *excluding* coda; shipped weights include
  an identical coda block (+645,312) → 1,710,049. Their generate.py models
  the pure-loop story and therefore cannot load the release.

